# Pwn4C drone – SSH authorized keys
#
# DEFAULT: empty (no pre-installed key). The drone ships with NO root password
# and NO authorized keys. The automation workflow must push a key before
# deploying to an untrusted network.
#
# HOW TO ADD A KEY (choose one):
#
#   A) Via the initial passwordless session (post-infect, pre-deployment):
#      ssh-copy-id -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub root@192.168.4.1
#
#   B) Via SCP:
#      scp ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub root@192.168.4.1:/etc/dropbear/authorized_keys
#      ssh root@192.168.4.1 "chmod 600 /etc/dropbear/authorized_keys"
#
#   C) Bake a key into the image (team deployments):
#      Copy your public key into:
#        firmware/files/etc/dropbear/authorized_keys
#      and rebuild the image. The key will land here at bake time.
#      WARNING: keys baked into a public repository are public. Use a
#      deployment-only key pair and rotate regularly.
#
# After adding a key, set a strong root password to disable passwordless login:
#   ssh root@192.168.4.1 "passwd root"
